'' A MACRO DEFINED IN A SUB IS SCOPED TO IT even when the SUB then declares a procedure-
'' pointer variable -- measured with fbc-modern: it prints 1, 2 and 'M scoped'. The
'' preprocessor counted 'as sub( )' as an opened SUB, so 'end sub' closed that instead,
'' M outlived a( ), and b( )'s '#define M 2' was TKO0305, "macro 'm' is already defined".
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/macro-scope-procptr.bas -o tests/driver/macroscopeprocptr.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/driver/macroscopeprocptr.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 1
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 2
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: M scoped
